<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>Ghent Guide: 20 Highlights &amp; Hidden Gems – Graslei, Gravensteen, Graffiti Lane – HiddenGem.Atlas</name><description>https://noelsprick-alt.github.io/HiddenGem.Atlas/en/guide/ghent/</description><Style id="must"><IconStyle><color>ff4cd8ff</color><Icon><href>https://maps.google.com/mapfiles/kml/paddle/wht-blank.png</href></Icon></IconStyle></Style><Style id="gem"><IconStyle><color>ffd0569b</color><Icon><href>https://maps.google.com/mapfiles/kml/paddle/wht-blank.png</href></Icon></IconStyle></Style><Placemark><name>1. St Michael’s Bridge – the three-towers view</name><styleUrl>#must</styleUrl><description>Must-see · 🆓 Free to experience · Stand in the middle of the bridge and shoot towards the north-east. With a wide-angle lens – the standard camera on many phones – all three towers fit in. The Graslei is only a few steps from here. · https://noelsprick-alt.github.io/HiddenGem.Atlas/en/guide/ghent/#o1</description><Point><coordinates>3.72056,51.05387,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>2. Graslei and Korenlei</name><styleUrl>#must</styleUrl><description>Must-see · 🆓 Free to experience · Come to the Graslei at night on your first evening – the lights on the façades make the best photo. By day it gets crowded; in the evening the quays are much quieter. · https://noelsprick-alt.github.io/HiddenGem.Atlas/en/guide/ghent/#o2</description><Point><coordinates>3.72077,51.05481,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>3. Korenmarkt, St Nicholas’ Church &amp; the old post office</name><styleUrl>#must</styleUrl><description>Must-see · 🆓 Free to experience · If you pass by in the evening: the view down the street with the church and belfry lit up is a classic – especially with the tram tracks in the foreground. · https://noelsprick-alt.github.io/HiddenGem.Atlas/en/guide/ghent/#o3</description><Point><coordinates>3.72289,51.05398,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>4. Town hall (Stadhuis)</name><styleUrl>#must</styleUrl><description>Must-see · 🆓 Free to experience · Walk all the way around the building before you take photos. In the morning the light on the Gothic façade is best, and on weekdays before 9 am you are almost alone. · https://noelsprick-alt.github.io/HiddenGem.Atlas/en/guide/ghent/#o4</description><Point><coordinates>3.72527,51.05453,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>5. Belfry (Belfort)</name><styleUrl>#must</styleUrl><description>Must-see · Go right at opening at 10 am: fewer people, better light. In July and August it pays to book online, otherwise you may wait 20–30 minutes. · https://noelsprick-alt.github.io/HiddenGem.Atlas/en/guide/ghent/#o5</description><Point><coordinates>3.72468,51.05363,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>7. Gravensteen – the castle of the counts</name><styleUrl>#must</styleUrl><description>Must-see · You do not have to choose a time slot, but booking online is worthwhile in high season. Plan 1.5–2 hours and go early in the day or shortly before closing. · https://noelsprick-alt.github.io/HiddenGem.Atlas/en/guide/ghent/#o7</description><Point><coordinates>3.72077,51.05718,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>8. Groentenmarkt &amp; Groot Vleeshuis</name><styleUrl>#must</styleUrl><description>Must-see · 🆓 Free to experience · Plan the Groentenmarkt as a stop between the Gravensteen and the Graslei – three Ghent specialities (mustard, cuberdons, genever) are within a few metres of each other here. · https://noelsprick-alt.github.io/HiddenGem.Atlas/en/guide/ghent/#o8</description><Point><coordinates>3.72168,51.05592,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>9. Werregarenstraatje – the legal graffiti lane</name><styleUrl>#gem</styleUrl><description>Hidden gem · 🆓 Free to experience · Come by day when artists are working – then you see the walls emerging. The motif changes constantly, so photograph everything right away. Ask sprayers briefly before photographing them from the front. · https://noelsprick-alt.github.io/HiddenGem.Atlas/en/guide/ghent/#o9</description><Point><coordinates>3.72463,51.05542,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>10. St Peter’s Abbey – a calm abbey with an orchard</name><styleUrl>#gem</styleUrl><description>Hidden gem · 🆓 Free to experience · Plan the abbey as a stop when arriving or leaving – it lies on the route between station and centre and is one of the calmest places in the city. · https://noelsprick-alt.github.io/HiddenGem.Atlas/en/guide/ghent/#o10</description><Point><coordinates>3.72669,51.04232,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>11. Groot Begijnhof Sint-Elisabeth – Ghent’s quiet World Heritage corner</name><styleUrl>#gem</styleUrl><description>Hidden gem · 🆓 Free to experience · Perfect for a quiet morning when you have had enough of the crowds in the old town. Rent a bike (one day is included with the City Card) and combine it with a café stop on the way back. · https://noelsprick-alt.github.io/HiddenGem.Atlas/en/guide/ghent/#o11</description><Point><coordinates>3.74754,51.05688,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>12. Patershol – Ghent’s medieval quarter</name><styleUrl>#must</styleUrl><description>Must-see · 🆓 Free to experience · Reserve ahead at weekends, the good restaurants fill up quickly. Try waterzooi once and stoverij once – then you have had both typical Ghent dishes. · https://noelsprick-alt.github.io/HiddenGem.Atlas/en/guide/ghent/#o12</description><Point><coordinates>3.72263,51.05792,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>13. St James’ Church &amp; Vrijdagmarkt</name><styleUrl>#must</styleUrl><description>Must-see · 🆓 Free to experience · https://noelsprick-alt.github.io/HiddenGem.Atlas/en/guide/ghent/#o13</description><Point><coordinates>3.72765,51.05655,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>15. Tierenteyn-Verlent – Ghent mustard since 1790</name><styleUrl>#gem</styleUrl><description>Hidden gem · Take a small pot; it fits well in a shoe or the edge of a suitcase. The shop is small and often busy – best right after opening or shortly before closing. · https://noelsprick-alt.github.io/HiddenGem.Atlas/en/guide/ghent/#o15</description><Point><coordinates>3.72242,51.05563,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>18. ’t Dreupelkot – genever in over 200 flavours</name><styleUrl>#gem</styleUrl><description>Hidden gem · Ask for a taste before ordering and start with a mild flavour such as honey or caramel. · https://noelsprick-alt.github.io/HiddenGem.Atlas/en/guide/ghent/#o18</description><Point><coordinates>3.72234,51.05627,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>19. Dulle Griet – 1.5 litres of beer in a boot</name><styleUrl>#must</styleUrl><description>Must-see · Wear a pair of shoes you can part with that evening. · https://noelsprick-alt.github.io/HiddenGem.Atlas/en/guide/ghent/#o19</description><Point><coordinates>3.72527,51.05657,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>20. Stadsbrouwerij Gruut – beer with herbs instead of hops</name><styleUrl>#gem</styleUrl><description>Hidden gem · Come in the afternoon and try a beer that does not taste of classic hops – for beer fans an interesting counterpoint to the Dulle Griet. · https://noelsprick-alt.github.io/HiddenGem.Atlas/en/guide/ghent/#o20</description><Point><coordinates>3.73023,51.05754,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark></Document></kml>
